From: lyq1996 <lyq123233@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: support access point firmware variants

Add a chip variant flag for access point firmware (selected by the
realtek,ap-firmware devicetree property), supporting per-RFE BB/RF/power
table sets, AP PLE/HFC quota overrides, eFEM RX gain parsing, RFE GPIO
routing, DFS radar detection widths for 20/40/80/160 MHz AP mode, SWSI
write readback verification, and skipping client-only scan offload,
PHY capability queries, and Bluetooth coexistence.

Let mac80211 compute the BIP MIC in software, since the access point
firmware has no management frame protection offload.

Apply the devicetree ieee80211-freq-limit property, and drop the 6 GHz
band when it leaves no usable 6 GHz channel, so that boards without a
6 GHz front-end do not register the band. The band's sband, channels,
bitrates and iftype_data are devm allocations, so release them with
devm_kfree() instead of kfree().

Signed-off-by: lyq1996 <lyq123233@163.com>
---
Index: backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/cam.c
===================================================================
--- backports-7.2.orig/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/cam.c
+++ backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/cam.c
@@ -515,6 +515,7 @@ int rtw89_cam_sec_key_add(struct rtw89_d
 		break;
 	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_AES_CMAC:
 		hw_key_type = RTW89_SEC_KEY_TYPE_BIP_CCMP128;
+		key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_MMIE;
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
